course: dictionary
lesson: 9642
title: Stupidly and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on where you find them, and «stupidly» is one of these. Its main meaning is in a silly or unwise way, without thinking first. «I stupidly left my coat at school» means the speaker made a careless mistake and feels a bit silly about it.
explain: Read the words around it to find the right meaning. In «staring stupidly up into the sky», the word staring shows a dazed, blank look, so stupidly means in a blank way with no thought behind it. In «stupidly expensive», there is no silliness at all: it means extremely expensive, so you could swap in very.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. Is someone making a bad choice, admitting a mistake, or just going very far? Then do a quick swap check: put very or foolishly in place of stupidly and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Stupidly is an adverb, so it tells us how something is done: stupidly, more stupidly, most stupidly.
fact: Meaning 1: «I stupidly left my coat at school» means in an unwise way, without thinking first.
fact: Meaning 2: «staring stupidly» means looking in a dazed, blank way.
fact: Meaning 3 (informal): «that ride was stupidly fun» means extremely fun, like really in slang.
fact: Use stupidly to admit your own small mistake. Do not use it to call other people stupid.
exercise: «I stupidly left my coat at school.» What does stupidly mean here? | In a very quick way | In a quiet, gentle way | * In a silly, unwise way, without thinking first | In a happy, joyful way
exercise: In «staring stupidly up into the sky», what kind of look does stupidly show? | A cross, angry look | A bright, cheerful look | * A dazed, blank look | A quick, sneaky look
exercise: Jamie says, «That ride was stupidly fun.» What does stupidly mean here? | Silly and unwise | Very slowly | * Extremely, like really | Not at all
test: Which sentence uses stupidly the right way, to admit a small mistake about yourself? | Stupidly, the teacher is always kind | * I stupidly forgot my swimming kit | The dog is stupidly lazy, so it sleeps all day | You are stupidly slow, Sam
test: In «stupidly expensive», what does stupidly mean? | * Extremely | Slowly and quietly | In a blank, dazed way | In a silly, unwise way
exam: Which swap check best shows that stupidly means extremely in «that ride was stupidly fun»? | * Swap in very: that ride was very fun, and it still makes sense | Swap in slowly: that ride was slowly fun | Swap in sadly: that ride was sadly fun | Swap in quietly: that ride was quietly fun
